_score_mult_vs_hist":90.1,"_gate_fcf_yield":null,"_gp_fcf_yield":null,"_score_fcf_yield":null,"_gate_int_coverage":null,"_gp_int_coverage":null,"_score_int_coverage":null,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gate_accruals":-0.06002451116929419,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":86.1,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.05474797055472791,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":98.6,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.0430938479756551,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":46.1,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.06965682383626981,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":67.9,"_gate_rev_durability":0.11979900308331248,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":84.9,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.09536354005907516,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.029676944818286533,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":87.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.02306276835003067,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":61.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.5016,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Morningstar, Inc. provides independent investment insights for investors in the United States, Asia, Australia, Canada, Continental Europe, the United Kingdom, and internationally. It operates through five segments: Morningstar Direct Platform, PitchBook, Morningstar Credit, Morningstar Wealth, and Morningstar Retirement. The company offers managed investments, including mutual funds, exchanged traded funds, separate accounts, collective investment trusts, model portfolios, equities, and fixed-income securities; Morningstar Direct, an investment analysis and reporting application; and Morningstar Advisor Workstation, a suite of tools to provide advice to clients. It also provides PitchBook that offers data and research covering the private capital markets comprising venture capital, private equity and credit, bank loans, and merger and acquisition activities through the PitchBook platform; Morningstar Model Portfolios, an advisor service with model portfolios for fee-based financial advisors; Morningstar International Wealth Platform, which offers discretionary asset management services; and Morningstar Investor/Morningstar.com, an individual investor platform and media site. In addition, the company offers credit ratings, research, data, and credit analytics solutions through Morningstar DBRS and Morningstar Credit Analytics agencies. Further, it provides managed retirement accounts, fiduciary services, and custom models; Morningstar Sustainalytics that provides environmental, social and governance data, research, and ratings; and Morningstar Indexes that offers market indexes used for performance benchmarks and as the basis for investment products and other portfolio strategies. The company was incorporated in 1984 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kunal  Kapoor C.F.A., CFA | CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $2.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 10K people. Revenue per employee of $223K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 10%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $40K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 13\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Morningstar, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $9.1B market cap on $2.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 9% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $443M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 18 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.58\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 14\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 9.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 50% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7063662041779196},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $27.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (45% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","15 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Joseph D. Mansueto Executes Sale of 7,250 Morningstar Shares on November 5, 2026 Under Rule 10b5-1 Plan","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/joseph-d-mansueto-executes-sale-of-7250-morningstar-shares-on-november-5-2026-under-rule-10b5-1-plan","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794007805.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Cathie Wood buys $47 million of popular semiconductor stock","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/cathie-wood-buys-47-million-200700000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794007106.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"ProShares to Launch ANTU and ANTY E